# Fusion 360 DXF Batch Export - AI Agent Guidelines

## API Reference
When working with Fusion 360 API code, always reference the official API documentation:
- **Fusion API Reference Repository**: https://github.com/AutodeskFusion360/FusionAPIReference
- This repository contains HTML documentation, C++ headers, and Python object definitions
- Use the Python reference in `Fusion_API_Python_Reference/defs/` for method signatures and properties
- Check `Fusion_API_Documentation/files/` for detailed API documentation

## Project Context
This is a Fusion 360 add-in script for batch exporting sheet metal flat patterns to DXF format with settings optimized for West Corte.

## Code Style
- Use the Fusion 360 Python API (`adsk.core`, `adsk.fusion`, `adsk.cam`)
- Follow existing error handling patterns with try/except blocks
- Include user-friendly error messages via `ui.messageBox()`
- Sanitize file names to replace illegal characters (e.g., `:` → `_`)

## Key API Classes Used
- `adsk.core.Application` - Main application access
- `adsk.fusion.Design` - Design document
- `adsk.fusion.Component` - Component objects
- `adsk.fusion.FlatPattern` - Flat pattern objects
- `adsk.fusion.ExportManager` - Export functionality
- `adsk.fusion.DXFFlatPatternExportOptions` - DXF export options
